From 21261acf0d115573b11976852acee2d6308ac767 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <jufangjian@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:51:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [rh2-integration] promote rollout-fn shutdown residue to a
 run failure verdict

close_rollout_fn_and_rh2 now turns any aclose() residue (deadline exceeded,
worker/active groups unfinished, close error, buffer not closed, aclose
raised) into a typed ShutdownFailure that becomes the rh2 first cause when
nothing else failed and a persisted secondary cause otherwise; concrete
unfinished group facts flow into the rh2 report residue so ok=false.
Cause precedence: in-flight driver exception is primary, worker/cleanup
failures secondary, same-origin wrappers deduplicated. RolloutManager.
dispose() returns a serialisable verdict (ok/cleanup_ok/timed_out/errors/
causes); train_async raises ShutdownFailure on a non-ok verdict when no
driver error is in flight (non-zero exit) and otherwise re-raises the
original while persisting a shutdown_failure.json marker. Normal
cancellation keeps ok=true.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
